# wiki-ai-thinkers — gitignore.
# Approach: blocklist of personal / large / ephemeral content. Everything
# else ships. The README and LICENSE-content.txt document what is and is
# not included.

# ---- Personal tool state -----------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.claudian/
.remember/

# ---- Obsidian per-user state ------------------------------------------------
# Keep the .obsidian config (themes, hotkeys) so cloners get the same
# graph/reading-mode settings. Exclude only the per-user workspace state.
.obsidian/workspace
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache

# ---- Working areas (personal, in flux) --------------------------------------
00_Inbox/
60_Drafts/
70_Research/
100_HTML_Artefacts/

# ---- Large binary caches (rebuild from canonical_url; see README) -----------
80_Attachments/
20_People/*/papers/

# ---- Per-thinker automation state (machine-generated; not portable) --------
99_Meta/wiki-thinkers/state/
99_Meta/wiki-thinkers/queries/

# ---- Stale meta artefacts from a previous vault layout ---------------------
# build_summary.py hardcodes a path to a different (older) vault; summary.docx
# is its stale output.
99_Meta/build_summary.py
99_Meta/summary.docx

# ---- Auto-generated wiki internals (per-run reports and quarantine) --------
_wiki/_reports/
_wiki/_quarantine/

# ---- Loose planning artefacts at vault root --------------------------------
# Inspiration / planning material that informed the design but is not the
# vault itself.
kaparthy-pattern.txt
*.canvas

# ---- OS / editor noise ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
